{"id": "instruction_15", "type": "instruction", "text": "<p><b>How you respond in this version.</b> Instead of clicking on the displays, you will use <b>sliders</b>. For each location you set an <b>x</b> slider (0 = left, 100 = right) and a <b>y</b> slider (0 = bottom, 100 = top): one x/y pair for the figure the speaker means in <b>Display A</b>, one pair for <b>Display B</b>, and one pair for the speaker's <b>blind spot</b>.</p>"}
{"id": "comprehension_quiz_01", "type": "comprehension_quiz", "text": "<p>Please answer all of the questions below to continue.</p>", "queries": [{"prompt": "How many cells can the collaborator see in each display?", "type": "multi-choice", "tag": "quiz_q1", "option": ["4", "3", "2", "1"], "answer": 1, "required": true}, {"prompt": "Does the collaborator know about the blind spot?", "type": "multi-choice", "tag": "quiz_q2", "option": ["Yes, exactly", "No, they do not know about it", "Only sometimes"], "answer": 1, "required": true}, {"prompt": "Within a trial, is the blind spot the same for Displays A and B?", "type": "multi-choice", "tag": "quiz_q3", "option": ["Yes", "No"], "answer": 0, "required": true}, {"prompt": "What does the x slider represent?", "type": "multi-choice", "tag": "quiz_q4", "option": ["0 is left and 100 is right", "0 is bottom and 100 is top", "It measures confidence only"], "answer": 0, "required": true}, {"prompt": "What does the y slider represent?", "type": "multi-choice", "tag": "quiz_q5", "option": ["0 is bottom and 100 is top", "0 is left and 100 is right", "It measures confidence only"], "answer": 0, "required": true}, {"prompt": "What is your task on each trial?", "type": "multi-choice", "tag": "quiz_q6", "option": ["Place approximate clicks for both referents and the blind spot", "Count how many shapes appear", "Describe the displays in your own words"], "answer": 0, "required": true}]}
